{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the S1 repair at head d6360231, tree e2044ee3, for request 449c58c7 and review request e49fdc81. Verdict: APPROVED, for landing.\n\nI reviewed the diff from 9b428613 against my f23c7342. My earlier conclusions on the production changes and the third room stand, and this head changes neither.\n\n## My five items\n\n1. A deployment during a run. The runbook now says that no Worker may deploy between the first phase and the last, and that a deployment in that window leaves no `check` or `continue` path. The note corrects its limit and says that the script doesn't enforce the rule.\n2. `name`. The runbook says that the input labels the room, that the home binds a run to its room, and that S2 to S9 take their references from the owner's private `s1-room-refs`.\n3. Source condition. The runbook requires a clean checkout at the reviewed commit, unchanged until `verify-seed` exits.\n4. Closing the witness. A new section says that every phase must exit 0 or complete by `continue`. It names the three receipts to read, and it says that no final phase shows this.\n5. Commands. The runbook leads with one command per phase from `owner`, and it states the `--diagnostics` parent and `.config` rules. `all` is named with the fact that it has never closed.\n\nThe note also carries the power-loss limit, the wrong-origin limit and the first meeting with later Workers. The runbook tells the reader to check `providerOrigin` first.\n\nOne point that doesn't block: the runbook says that a stop under `all` names the phase. `setup.ts:93` prints the current phase, and my reader found that a failure before the loop can print `all`. A person who sees that can start from `owner` with `check`.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The gate at 9bc8c663, tree 8c2ba946, exits 0: Plain 3,236 with one skip, Native 900 with two skips. It includes main 76cac675. From there to this head, only the note and the manifest change.\n- From 42099ef1 to that checkpoint, the only path under `examples`, `packages/cli` or `packages/client` that changes is `runbook.md`. So the third room's evidence carries, as the note says, with the limit that the room ran at 4b9e1a89 on Worker da13242c.\n- The evidence verifies. All 6 manifest rows match, the directory holds 38 files with none writable, and `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean with digest 99007a2a.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree` of main 0583803c and this head completes without conflict. The merge adds only the sprint report.\n- `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, `check-doc-links` finds 779 links with 0 broken, `check-commit-messages` passes, `git diff --check` is clean, and the worktree stayed clean.\n\nI ran no test on this tail, since no source changed, and no live act. I didn't read the owner's `s1-done-*` files; the builder counted them by name.\n\n## For the planner\n\n- The enrollment stop still has no owner. Filing a request or accepting the limit is your decision, and the note records that.\n- The real run comes after the post-J4 deployment and meets the later landings for the first time. Hold deployments for the whole of that run.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved. The script uses the existing Register and the J4 definitions, and it changes no service default.\n- Security: approved. No authority widens, checker issuance stays separate, and retained originals are reused and not re-signed.\n- Simplification: approved for landing. The redundant checks I listed can go in a later change.\n- Deployment: no deployment follows from this landing. The real room is the planner's run.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e73e283265cc7ec1dbe7e0e5fd0da1a3e59c1d0a","binding":"assigned","head":"d63602318c4cd4bd8a31d565fd493dda25fd5318","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ffcdbe2b902757162d8b988139f2bb0038e649c6\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8a90580e1